The 1976 bracelet looked "like gold nuggets kind of hammered flat".<ref name = "becky" /> The bracelet in 1976 cost approximately $500. In the 1980s, [[Las Vegas, Nevada|Las Vegas]] jeweler Mordechai Yerushalmi became the exclusive manufacturer of WSOP bracelets until Harrah's Entertainment bought the rights to the WSOP in 2004.<ref name = "becky" /> According to 2003 WSOP Champion [[Chris Moneymaker]], the design of the bracelet remained relatively unchanged under Yerushalmi.<ref>ESPN's coverage of the 2007 World Series of Poker Episode 13</ref> In 2005, Gold and Diamond International based in Memphis, TN won the bid from Harrah's Entertainment to manufacture the 2005 World Series of Poker bracelets. The company also manufactures the WSOP circuit rings.<ref>CardPlayer Magazine</ref>

In 2006, Frederick Goldman, Inc. made the WSOP bracelets while luxury watch maker Corum introduced some commemorative watches as part of the prize package.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/tourney/updates.asp?tid=3461&grid=309|title=Limit Hold'em (Event 34)|work=World Series of Poker|publisher=Harrah's Entertainment|access-date=June 15, 2009}}{{Dead link|date=February 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokerpages.com/tournament/result20309.htm|title=39th World Series of Poker 2008|work=Poker Tournament Results|publisher=PokerPages|access-date=June 14, 2009|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090314054501/http://www.pokerpages.com/tournament/result20309.htm|archive-date=March 14, 2009|df=mdy-all}}</ref> In 2006, the Champion's bracelet had 259 stones including 7.2 carats (1.4 g) of diamonds, 120 grams of white and yellow gold. It also used rubies to represent the heart and diamond suits, a sapphire to represent the spade and three black diamonds to represent the clubs.<ref name = "becky" />

In 2007, Corum became the official bracelet manufacturer for the WSOP. Some of the 2007 World Series of Poker champions received both a watch and a bracelet from Corum. Corum designed four variations for the 2007 World Series of Poker Bracelets. The standard version that is presented to 53 winners features 53 diamonds.<ref name="corum">[http://www.globeinvestor.com/servlet/story/BWIRE.20070605.20070605006220/GIStory CORUM Introduces New World Series of Poker(R) Bracelets] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091211213804/http://www.globeinvestor.com/servlet/story/BWIRE.20070605.20070605006220/GIStory |date=December 11, 2009 }} June 5, 2007. ''GlobalInvestor''  Accessed July 30, 2007</ref> The Ladies World Champion receives a bracelet that is adorned with four black diamonds, two rubies and 87 blue sapphires.<ref>Press Release. [http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/news/varchive.asp?aid=1021 Poker Academy Student Bests Largest-Ever Field To Become 2007 World Series of Poker Ladies Champion] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070711023153/http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/news/varchive.asp?aid=1021 |date=July 11, 2007 }} June 13, 2007. ''WorldSeriesofPoker.com'' Accessed July 7, 2007</ref> The $50,000 HORSE Champion Bracelet has 91 black diamonds and two rubies.<ref name="Corum">Press Release.[http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/news/varchive.asp?aid=824 CORUM Introduces New World Series of Poker Bracelets; Elegant Design Features 18 Carat Gold, Precious Gems] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071007133009/http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/news/varchive.asp?aid=824 |date=October 7, 2007 }} June 5, 2007. ''WorldSeriesofPoker.com'' Accessed July 7, 2007</ref> The World Series of Poker Main Event Bracelet has 120 diamonds on 136 grams of 18-karat (75 percent) white gold.<ref name = "Corum" /> The value of the 2007 bracelets have not been released, but the typical price of a Corum watch ranges from $1,500–$30,000+.<ref>[http://www.nextag.com/corum-watch-men/search-html Corum pricelist per Next Tag] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070927010004/http://www.nextag.com/corum-watch-men/search-html |date=September 27, 2007 }} Accessed July 30, 2007</ref>

In 2008, the Main Event Bracelet had 291 diamonds, totalling 2.81 carats set in 168 grams of 18-karat white gold. The other 54 event bracelets consisted of 55 diamonds, totalling 0.25 carats set in 80 grams of 14-karat yellow gold.<ref>[http://www.vialuxe.com/News/Corum-Watches-Corum-2008-World-Series-of-Poker-Bracelets/1783,28977 Corum 2008 World Series of Poker Bracelets – ViaLuxe] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100223015311/http://www.vialuxe.com/News/Corum-Watches-Corum-2008-World-Series-of-Poker-Bracelets/1783,28977 |date=February 23, 2010 }}</ref>

In 2010, an Australian-based company OnTilt Designs Pty Ltd won a multi-year contract to become the official bracelet manufacturer for the WSOP. OnTilt jewelers decided that the 2010 bracelet design would return to the tradition of the 1970s and 1980s where the bracelet was a heavy piece of unadorned metal. American jewelry designer [[Steve Soffa]] was chosen to design and manufacture the entire set of bracelets.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gibson |first=Sean |date=14 May 2010 |title=WSOP Bracelet Designer Steve Soffa Interview |url=http://www.pokernewsdaily.com/wsop-bracelet-designer-steve-soffa-interview-11316/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140429193034/http://www.pokernewsdaily.com/wsop-bracelet-designer-steve-soffa-interview-11316/ |archive-date=April 29, 2014 |access-date=29 April 2014 |website=Poker News Daily |df=mdy-all}}</ref> The goal was to create a bracelet that somebody would actually want to wear every day. In 2011, OnTilt has also been chosen to manufacture the [[World Series of Poker Circuit events|WSOP Circuit]] rings.

In 2012, Jason Arasheben, famed jewelry designer and owner of Jason of Beverly Hills was chosen as the official bracelet manufacturer of the WSOP. Arasheben had designed the championship rings for the 2009 and 2010 Los Angeles Lakers and the 2011 Green Bay Packers, among others. The Main Event bracelet will feature each suit in the deck in either rubies or black diamonds. In terms of sheer mass, it weighs in at over 160 grams of 14 karat gold and over 35 carats of flawless diamonds.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bluff.com/news/wsop-reveals-new-bracelet-design-by-jason-of-beverly-hills-26967/ |title=WSOP Reveals New Bracelet Design by Jason of Beverly Hills |access-date=2013-06-10 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140706124628/http://www.bluff.com/news/wsop-reveals-new-bracelet-design-by-jason-of-beverly-hills-26967/ |archive-date=July 6, 2014 |df=mdy-all }}</ref>

A special platinum bracelet was awarded at the 2012 WSOP to the winner of The [[Big One for One Drop]], Antonio Esfandiari. The event was a $1 million buy-in tournament created as a fundraiser for the [[One Drop Foundation]], a charity established by [[Cirque du Soleil]] founder [[Guy Laliberté]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.espn.com/poker/story/_/id/7804846/world-series-poker-offer-1-million-buy-tournament |title=WSOP to offer $1 million buy-in |agency=Associated Press |work=ESPN.com |date=April 12, 2012 |access-date=April 13, 2012 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120413123408/http://espn.go.com/poker/story/_/id/7804846/world-series-poker-offer-1-million-buy-tournament |archive-date=April 13, 2012 |df=mdy-all }}</ref>

==Prestige==
At first, the bracelets did not have much prestige. Ten-time bracelet winner [[Doyle Brunson]] said that his first bracelet "didn't mean anything" to him and that he did not even pick up two of them.<ref name = "WSOP2007" />

Some professional poker players believe that there are two types of poker players: those who have won a bracelet and those who have not. Those who have belong to an exclusive club.<ref name = "WSOP2007" /> "It's impossible to overstate the value of a World Series of Poker gold bracelet to anyone who takes the game seriously," stated World Series of Poker Commissioner [[Jeffrey Pollack]] during the 2006 bracelet unveiling. "It is the equivalent of winning the [[Stanley Cup]] in [[ice hockey|hockey]] or the [[Vince Lombardi Trophy|Lombardi Trophy]] in [[American football]]."<ref>Burton, Earl. [http://www.pokernews.com/news/2006/6/world-series-poker-bracelet.htm 2006 World Series of Poker Bracelet Unveiled]. June 7, 2006. ''Pokernews.com'' Accessed July 30, 2007</ref>

Many professional poker players desire the recognition that is associated with the bracelet. Former [[Celebrity Poker Showdown]] host and poker star [[Phil Gordon (poker player)|Phil Gordon]] said, "I want that bracelet more than anything."<ref>[http://www.pokerlistings.com/phil-gordons-quest-for-a-wsop-bracelet-continues-734 Phil Gordon's Quest for a WSOP Bracelet Continues] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070927193038/http://www.pokerlistings.com/phil-gordons-quest-for-a-wsop-bracelet-continues-734 |date=September 27, 2007 }}. (June 10, 2005). ''Pokerlistings.com''.</ref> [[Freddy Deeb]] said that he did not appreciate his first bracelet because he did not recognize what it meant. He said his 2007 bracelet, however, "means everything to me".<ref>Press Release. [http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/news/varchive.asp?aid=1346 Freddy Deeb Wins $50,000 HORSE Championship at World Series of Poker Title Establishes Deeb as World's Best All-Around Player] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071007140018/http://www.worldseriesofpoker.com/news/varchive.asp?aid=1346 |date=October 7, 2007 }} June 29, 2007. ''WorldSeriesOfPoker.com'' Accessed July 30, 2007</ref> [[Jennifer Tilly]] says that winning her 2005 Women's Championship bracelet was "better than an [[Academy Award|Oscar]]".<ref name = "WSOP2007">ESPN's Coverage of the 2007 World Series of Poker, Episode 2</ref>

When the [[World Poker Tour]] decided to offer a prize to its event champions, they decided to present them with [[World Poker Tour bracelet|WPT Bracelets.]] In so doing, WPT Founder, President and CEO Steve Lipscomb said, "The championship bracelet has become synonymous with poker as a symbol of achievement and respect, and we are honored to continue the tradition that [[Benny Binion]] [the founder of the WSOP] began over 30 years ago."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/pressRelease/idUS132757+08-Apr-2008+BW20080408|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130201074437/http://www.reuters.com/article/pressRelease/idUS132757+08-Apr-2008+BW20080408|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 1, 2013|title=Six Seasons of Champions to Receive WPT Championship Bracelet|date=April 8, 2008|work=Reuters|access-date=February 11, 2009}}</ref>

==History==
Bracelets have not always been awarded for winning events. In 1970, the first WSOP Champion received nothing but a silver cup and whatever cash they won during the event.<ref>The first WSOP was not a freeze out tournament, but rather a collection of the top players playing against one another and the eventual winner was determined by a vote. [http://www.pokerplayerpress.com/Gallery-JohnnyMoss.html Johnny Moss Biography] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070811165953/http://www.pokerplayerpress.com/Gallery-JohnnyMoss.html |date=August 11, 2007 }} ''PokerPlayerPress.com''</ref> From 1971 to 1974, according to Becky Behnen (the daughter of WSOP founder [[Benny Binion]]), the winner received an undescribed "corny trophy".<ref name="becky">Associated Press [http://www.abqtrib.com/news/2006/jul/28/pokers-glory-is-about-the-bracelet-not-the-money/?printer=1/ Poker's glory is about the bracelet, not the money] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090422062532/http://www.abqtrib.com/news/2006/jul/28/pokers-glory-is-about-the-bracelet-not-the-money/?printer=1%2F |date=April 22, 2009 }} ''Albuquerque Tribune''. (July 28, 2006).</ref> In 1975, the winners received a sterling plate. In 1976, the WSOP started the tradition of issuing bracelets to the event winners.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2016-07-09 |title=Here's the deal about the World Series of Poker and bracelets |url=https://www.reviewjournal.com/life/heres-the-deal-about-the-world-series-of-poker-and-bracelets/ |access-date=2025-04-17 |website=Las Vegas Review-Journal |language=en-US}}</ref>

In 1980 and 1981, one did not have to win a WSOP event to win a gold bracelet. In 1980 and 1981, H.D. "Oklahoma Johny" Hale and [[Chip Reese]] received a gold bracelet for being the "Best All Around Player" at the WSOP, respectively.<ref>"Oklahoma Johnny" Hale.[http://gaming.unlv.edu/WSOP/Hale.pdf "Oklahoma Johnny" Hale.] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061208025543/http://gaming.unlv.edu/WSOP/Hale.pdf |date=December 8, 2006 }} '''The Life and Times of a Gentleman Gambler.''' Las Vegas: Poker Plus Publications, 1999. 127–132. Accessed July 12, 2007]</ref> These bracelets, however, are not considered in the count of WSOP championship bracelets.

In 2007, [[Thomas Bihl]] became the first person to ever win a WSOP bracelet outside [[Las Vegas Valley|Las Vegas]], Nevada. Bihl won the £2,500 World Championship H.O.R.S.E. at the [[World Series of Poker Europe]] in London, England.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokerlistings.com/poker-player-interviews/wsop/2007/send-the-bills-to-bihl-thomas-bihl-wins-wsope-event-1|title=Send the bills to Bihl! – Thomas Bihl wins WSOPE Event 1|work=Poker Listing|date=August 7, 2007|access-date=June 15, 2009|last=Crowson|first=Authur|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080717001619/http://www.pokerlistings.com/poker-player-interviews/wsop/2007/send-the-bills-to-bihl-thomas-bihl-wins-wsope-event-1|archive-date=July 17, 2008|df=mdy-all}}</ref> Days later, [[Annette Obrestad]] became the youngest player to ever win a WSOP bracelet at 18 years, 364 days, also becoming the first woman to win a World Series Main Event (WSOPE).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokernews.com/news/2007/09/wsope-event-3-final-table-annette-obrestad-wins.htm|work=Pokernews.com|title=£10,000 NLHE, Final Table: Annette Obrestad Makes History|date=September 17, 2007 |access-date=May 9, 2009|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090530144034/http://www.pokernews.com/news/2007/09/wsope-event-3-final-table-annette-obrestad-wins.htm|archive-date=May 30, 2009|df=mdy-all}}</ref> Caesars Entertainment (known until 2010 as Harrah's Entertainment), the owner of the WSOP, considers the WSOP Europe bracelet to be the same in prestige as those awarded every year in Las Vegas.

In 2008, [[Jesper Hougaard]] became the first person to have won both a WSOP and WSOPE bracelet.{{cn|date=January 2024}}

In 2011, a World Series of Poker bracelet was awarded for the first time to the [[World Series of Poker Circuit events|WSOP Circuit National Championship]] winner in the 100-qualifier event from May 27–29.<ref name="CNC"/><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.wsop.com/tourney/tourneydetails.asp?groupID=812|title=$1,000,000 WSOP Circuit NATIONAL CHAMPIONSHIP|access-date=June 5, 2011|date=May 29, 2001|publisher=Caesars Interactive Entertainment, Inc.|work=WSOP.com|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110717160438/http://www.wsop.com/tourney/tourneydetails.asp?groupID=812|archive-date=July 17, 2011|df=mdy-all}}</ref> The following year, the Circuit National Championship moved to [[Harrah's New Orleans|New Orleans]],<ref name="Feldman">{{cite news |url=https://www.espn.com/poker/story/_/id/6800493/2011-12-world-series-poker-circuit-schedule-feature-16-tour-stops |title='11-'12 WSOP Circuit to feature 16 stops |first=Andrew |last=Feldman |work=[[ESPN.com]] |date=July 29, 2011 |access-date=July 28, 2012 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111223115328/http://espn.go.com/poker/story/_/id/6800493/2011-12-world-series-poker-circuit-schedule-feature-16-tour-stops |archive-date=December 23, 2011 |df=mdy-all }}</ref> where it was held in 2013.<ref name="ESPN">{{cite news |url=https://www.espn.com/poker/story/_/id/8192752/2012-13-world-series-poker-circuit-schedule-feature-20-tour-stops |title=WSOP Circuit expands for 2012–13 |first=Andrew |last=Feldman |work=[[ESPN.com]] |date=July 23, 2012 |access-date=July 28, 2012 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120726014645/http://espn.go.com/poker/story/_/id/8192752/2012-13-world-series-poker-circuit-schedule-feature-20-tour-stops |archive-date=July 26, 2012 |df=mdy-all }}</ref>

Starting in 2013, bracelets are also awarded in Australia at the World Series of Poker Asia-Pacific, held at [[Crown Casino and Entertainment Complex|Crown Melbourne]].<ref name="WSOP APAC"/>

==Bracelet legacy==
Of the three top WSOP bracelet winners, only [[Johnny Chan (poker player)|Johnny Chan]] still has them all. He keeps them locked in a vault because they are worth, according to him, "millions".<ref name = "becky" /> Doyle Brunson did not pick up two of his. Seventeen-time bracelet winner [[Phil Hellmuth]] gave away ten of his. "To me," Hellmuth said, "the bracelets have always been a really huge deal, to me more than the other guys, because I knew that they represented history."<ref name = "becky" />

Three-time WSOP Bracelet winner [[Hamid Dastmalchi]] and six-time winner [[Ted Forrest]] had been playing for four days non-stop at [[the Mirage]] when Hamid started to complain about the 1992 Main Event Championship Bracelet he received. Bitter about a dispute with the [[Binion's Horseshoe]], the owners of the WSOP at the time, Hamid told the table that the Binion's "say it's worth $5,000, but I'd take $1,500 for it." To which Forrest responded "Sold" and immediately tossed Hamid $1,500 in chips. Dastmalchi mailed Forrest his bracelet.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokernewsdaily.com/ted-forrest-141/|title=Ted Forrest|work=Player Profile|date=July 15, 2008 |publisher=Poker News Daily|access-date=June 20, 2009|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090223231015/http://www.pokernewsdaily.com/ted-forrest-141/|archive-date=February 23, 2009|df=mdy-all}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fulltiltpoker.com/poker-blog/2009/06/767_2009_wsop_25_ghost_series_3_39_champions_part_iii.php|title=#767 – 2009 WSOP No. 25 – Ghost Series No. 3 – 39 Champions, Part III|last=Wilson|first=Craig|date=June 9, 2009|access-date=June 20, 2009|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090612052656/http://www.fulltiltpoker.com/poker-blog/2009/06/767_2009_wsop_25_ghost_series_3_39_champions_part_iii.php|archive-date=June 12, 2009|df=mdy-all}}</ref> Ted Forrest also reported that three of his five bracelets have been stolen over the years, and that he gave his daughter one.<ref>Administrator [http://www.ixgames.com/ted_forrest/ Ted Forrest Biography] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070928141633/http://www.ixgames.com/ted_forrest/ |date=September 28, 2007 }} ''IXGames'' Accessed July 30, 2007</ref>

In November 2010, [[Peter Eastgate]] put his main event bracelet up for auction on [[eBay]] with a starting bid of $16,000. It eventually sold for $147,500,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://poker-on-line.com/news/1011/peter-eastgate-2008-wsop-bracelet-sold.html|title=Peter Eastgate WSOP Bracelet Sold on ebay for $147,500|website=poker-on-line.com|access-date=August 9, 2017|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170810012226/http://poker-on-line.com/news/1011/peter-eastgate-2008-wsop-bracelet-sold.html|archive-date=August 10, 2017|df=mdy-all}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.pokernewsdaily.com/peter-eastgate-auctions-wsop-main-event-bracelet-for-147500-16980/|title=Peter Eastgate Auctions WSOP Main Event Bracelet for $147,500|date=November 25, 2010 |access-date=August 9, 2017|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170705121833/https://www.pokernewsdaily.com/peter-eastgate-auctions-wsop-main-event-bracelet-for-147500-16980/|archive-date=July 5, 2017|df=mdy-all}}</ref> and this money was donated to [[UNICEF]].<ref name="d281">{{cite web | last=Chaivarlis | first=Elaine | title=The Nightly Turbo: Peter Eastgate Auctions off WSOP Bracelet, APT Macau Crowns Winner, and More | website=PokerNews | date=2010-11-16 | url=https://www.pokernews.com/news/2010/11/the-nightly-turbo-peter-eastgate-auctions-of-wsop-bracelet-a-9333.htm | access-date=2024-11-12}}</ref>

==WSOP Circuit rings==
{{Unreferenced section|date=January 2024}}
In 2005, the inaugural [[World Series of Poker Circuit]] was founded, hosting events at many of their casinos around the country. In order to differentiate these events and to ensure the prestige of the WSOP Bracelet, the circuit events present a ring to the winners.<ref>{{Cite web |title=WSOP History |url=https://www.wsop.com/about/world-series-of-poker |access-date=2025-09-07 |website=WSOP.com |language=en}}</ref>

===Circuit National Championship===
{{Main|World Series of Poker Circuit#WSOP Circuit National Championship}}
From 2011, the WSOP awarded a bracelet to the winner of the WSOP Circuit National Championship. The Circuit Event National Championship was an invitation only event that used the standings of players from the various circuit events in determining who was invited.

